  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a0001cc40633e2242a75f7015c8a9162, type: 3}
  m_Name: Quest2_Level2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: "Quest 2 \xB7 Level 2"
  lockZoomOut: 0
  graphVariableMode: 11
  lockedScenario: 0
  lockedSpeedStep: -1
  graphSelectable: 0
  allowSideBySide: 0
  allowDifferentCubes: 1
  opening: Now that you have seen how fire disturbs each zone, let us look at how
    they RECOVER. Here recovery is measured by vegetation height - how long it takes
    for plants to grow back toward their pre-fire baseline. Explore each zone and
    compare how quickly, and how fully, they bounce back.
  ending: Great job! Note here that chaparral can regrow substantially within a decade
    or two if left undisturbed, but repeated fires, drought, or other climate events
    can slow or restart regrowth trajectories. Full recovery back to the pre-fire
    baseline can take much longer than the first flush of regrowth you see in the
    early years.
  defaultOptions: []
  questions:
  - prompt: Which zone shows the most limited height recovery? While answering, think
      about why that may be.
    options: []
    correctIndex: 0
    graphSelect: 0
    correctYearsByScenario: []
    textInput: 1
  - prompt: Which zone recovers most completely toward the pre-fire baseline? While
      answering, think about why that may be.
    options: []
    correctIndex: 0
    graphSelect: 0
    correctYearsByScenario: []
    textInput: 1
  - prompt: Compare zone-to-zone (side by side North vs South) to hone in on the
      message that they differ comparatively, after they have explored each of them
      individually.
    options: []
    correctIndex: 0
    graphSelect: 0
    correctYearsByScenario: []
    textInput: 0
